> Tru64, and my ultimate goal is to add that space to an existing File 
> Domain (usr_domain) which /usr and /var are housed on.  I have purchased 
> the ADVFS utilities and have them installed.  However, I need some 
> assistance in making Tru64 see the extra space.  Can someone please 
> advise me as to my next steps, or a FAQ/article to read over.  Thank you 
> for your time!

Not sure why you would want to add mirrored storage into the same file domain 
with non-mirrored storage.  If you lose one of the non-mirrored internal drives, 
you still have to rebuild the entire domain from backups.  You'd be better off 
creating a separate file domain for the protected storage, and hosting critical 
data in it, leaving easily-rebuilt stuff in the usr_domain.  (Or attaching your 
internal drives to the kzpac as well, and rebuilding everything.)

That aside, your OS won't see your new raid controller until you build a new 
kernel.  Not sure about 5.1, but under 4.0 this was accomplished by rebooting 
with a kernel of /genvmunix to detect the new hardware, and then runnning 
doconfig to create a new config file & kernel.  Once you've got the correct 
entry for the kzpac, you can add logical drives to the o/s in the future by just 
manually editing the config file and building.



