I just wanted to close this out.  I believe I got this working!  Thanks 
to everyone that helped.

The key was /dev/disk/dsk1c , that was where Tru64 found the new space. 
    This was found out by going in through sys manager and going in 
through Hardware, and selecting Device Information.

Next I went and used disklabel -wr /dev/disk/dsk1c
Then did disklabel -t advfs

Then simply use addvol /dev/disk/dsk1c usr_vol

More space was added!

I appreciate everyone helping.  I am still relatively new to Tru64, and 
appreciate everyone's patience as well.

