> My Alpha Server 1200 has 5.1A TRU64 installed. Anybody know if it is
> possible to install another OS version 5.1B in another disk on this
> machine? How to boot the system from a device different from default?
>
> Thanks.

The general boot command for unix is:

>>> b -fl a dka300

where dka300 is the target system disk. Your possibilities are listed in:

>>> show dev

Boot into single user mode with:

>>> b -fl s dka300

If you have VMS on another disk note that the boot flags are different:

>>> b -fl 0,0 dkc200

The first 0 points to the system root to boot from (i.e. SYS0), the second 0
is a
parameter that allows you to boot converstationally:

>>> b -fl 0,1 dkc200

If you want to boot WindowsNT then you need to start AlphaBIOS first, IIRC:

>>> AlphaBIOS

Hans




