Emanuele wrote:
> Hi,
> how  do i do a full backup on tru 64 unix?
> Thanks
> 
> 

Use vdump and vrestore.  We put a tar file at the beginning of our tapes 
that contain information required to fully restore the system, such as 
hostname, df -k, file domain info, and any utilities required to 
configure the system.

One such utility is vrestore itself.  This may seem silly, since 
vrestore comes on the boot cd, however one of the patch kits updates 
vdump and vrestore enough that the vrestore on the cdrom no longer reads 
the vdump files made by the patched vdump.  Put the patched vrestore in 
your tar file.

Mario



